// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 12-type-system
// facility: rule.fn.generic-call [Generic-Call-Uninferable] (an argument of another generic call); conf.generic-call-uninferable-in-generic-argument
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.cannot-infer-type-parameter (static)
//
// `make()`, whose `T` occurs in no argument, only in its result: as the
// argument of `Vec::len`, whose own `T` is not yet known, the expected type
// cannot fix it, so the call is uninferable, and is rejected as it is as a
// statement. (Before the session findings of 2026-11-06 an expected type
// that was not yet fixed deferred the question for every parameter, and
// nothing asked it again: the program was accepted, and it ran. The case
// used `Result::unwrap` of an `Option` until report 117 of Update 207 made
// that a `diag.type-mismatch` naming `Option::unwrap`.)

import std;

fn make<T>() : Vec<T>
{
    Vec::new()
}

fn main() : u8
{
    usize n = Vec::len(&make());
    printf("%v\n", n);
    0
}
